/target
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
.claude_consciousness.m8
.omo/

# --- Local-artifact guards -------------------------------------------------
# e9d8fa9 committed 24 Windows process environment dumps into the pager crate:
# a WSL-side tool wrote Win32 paths verbatim, so `C:\Users\...\Temp\.tmpXXXX`
# landed as a *literal filename* in the repo root of that crate and `git add -A`
# swept it up. The dumps contained live API keys. Block the shape, not the
# instance — none of these patterns can ever match real source.
**/C:*
**/*Temp.tmp*
**/.tmp[A-Za-z0-9]*
**/env.txt
**/*env.txt

# Environment files. .env.example is the documented template and stays tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Credential material. Nothing in this workspace legitimately carries these
# extensions; a match is an accident, not a build input.
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa
id_ed25519
credentials.json
auth.json
.npmrc
